================================================================================
Lakebase registry store: share registry id + lazy-heal flags process-wide
================================================================================

Context:
LakebaseRegistryStore is rebuilt on every request (RegistryService.from_context,
EditLockService._store, ...), but its resolved registry id and its lazy-heal
guards ("does column/table X exist?") lived on the instance. Every request
therefore re-ran the registries lookup plus up to three information_schema
probes before the real query (~150 ms per round-trip from a dev laptop):
e.g. POST /domain/edit-lock/renew p50 458 ms for a single UPDATE.
Controlled read-only A/B on the dev Lakebase (fresh store, list_versions +
read_version, the core of load-from-uc): p50 997 ms -> 310 ms.

Changes:
1. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py
   - New _SharedStoreState descriptor + _SHARED_STATE map keyed by
     (database override, schema). _registry_id and the 16 lazy-heal flags
     (_status_column_ready, _edit_locks_ready, ...) are now class-level
     descriptors backed by that shared dict; __init__ binds
     self._shared_state instead of resetting each attribute.
   - Instances built via __new__ (no __init__) fall back to plain
     per-instance attributes.
   - LakebaseRegistryStore.reset_shared_state(database=None, schema=None)
     clears state in place (live instances keep their dict reference).
2. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/Bootstrap.py
   - initialize() clears the shared state first so the registry id and
     column/table guards are re-probed after (re)provisioning.
3. src/back/objects/domain/settings/graphengine/GraphEngineLakebaseSettings.py
   - After an admin DROP SCHEMA/TABLE/VIEW, reset the shared store state
     (the dropped object may back the registry). Nested `with` merged so
     the class does not grow (architecture size budget).
4. src/api/routers/internal/domain.py
   - POST /domain/load-from-uc: edit-lock orchestration
     (release_prev_on_switch, on_domain_loaded, reacquire) now runs through
     run_blocking, like the load itself.
5. tests/conftest.py
   - Autouse fixture resets the shared store state around every test.
6. tests/units/registry/test_lakebase_store_shared_state.py (new)
   - Sharing across instances, isolation per schema/database, single
     registry lookup for many instances, in-place reset, targeted reset,
     initialize() forgets cached state, __new__ fallback.
7. tests/units/registry/test_mcp_policy_column.py
   - Memoisation contract now checks the shared descriptor declaration.

