================================================================================
Delta engine: Certified Graph composition objects
================================================================================

Context:
Third step toward the two-phase graph. The Certified Graph is composed in
Delta for every backend: a base VIEW over the Original `…_data` (no copy),
an enrichments TABLE that carries `kind` / `provenance` / `run_id`, and a
union VIEW that is the certified content. This change adds the naming, the
DDL and the Delta builder entry point; nothing calls it yet (the certified
build comes next). The composition lives in the Delta engine and is reached
through `GraphDBFactory.get_builder(engine="delta")`, so no class in
`back/objects` merely forwards to it.

Changes:
1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/_table_naming.py
   - `cert_base_fqn`, `cert_enriched_fqn`, `certified_view_fqn`
     (`…_cert_base`, `…_cert_enriched`, `…_certified`); the three suffixes
     are stripped by `strip_graph_leaf_suffix`.
   - Duplicated Code: `data_table_fqn`, `inferred_table_fqn` and
     `graph_view_fqn` share the new `_suffixed_fqn` helper.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/materialize.py
   - `build_ensure_cert_enriched_sql`: enrichments TABLE (subject,
     predicate, object, kind, provenance, run_id, created_at).
   - `ensure_certified_composition`: base VIEW over `…_data`, enrichments
     TABLE (create once, never cleared), union VIEW base ∪ enrichments.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/Builder.py
   - `cert_base_fqn`, `cert_enriched_fqn`, `certified_view_fqn`,
     `ensure_certified_composition`.
