================================================================================
Certified build: compose in Delta, load Lakebase / Neo4j from the composition
================================================================================

Context:
Fourth step toward the two-phase graph. New sub-package
`back/objects/digitaltwin/certify/` with `CertifiedBuild`, which builds the
Certified Graph of a domain version from its Original Graph: it creates the
Delta composition, then either serves it as is (Lakehouse virtual) or loads
the domain's graph engine from `…_cert_base` with `GraphLoad` (Lakebase
app_managed, Neo4j). The run is recorded in `build_runs` with
`build_kind = certified`. Not wired to a route yet. Lakehouse materialized
and Lakebase managed_synced are refused with a clear message for now (they
need `…_cert_data` and an `object_hash` source view respectively).

