External reads serve PUBLISHED versions only (REST v1, external GraphQL, MCP)
================================================================================

Context:
Decision D4 of the certified-graph SPEC, applied to the whole REST v1
surface (MCP is one of its clients). External reads used to load the
numeric-latest version of any lifecycle status. They now load the
numeric-latest PUBLISHED version, accept an explicit version only when it is
PUBLISHED (404 otherwise), and need a context (`domain_name`, or one open in
the session; 400 otherwise). The domain listing only shows domains with a
PUBLISHED version. Writes reached through REST v1 (build, data-quality /
inference starts, cohort dry-run / materialize, entity business rules) are
unchanged here; they move with the writes step. Reading the Certified Graph
itself (variant) is the next step.

